[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Objectives

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
1. Forecast the next trading day's price change of a configured security and offer the forecast through an API and a web app.
2. Keep the forecast current without manual steps: new quotes arrive, the model is retrained, a better model replaces the current one, and the running system is monitored for data drift and service health.
3. Compare every model honestly against simple baselines and state clearly that the service is not investment advice.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Key metrics

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Model quality, measured on data the model has not seen, ordered by time:

- Mean absolute error (MAE) of the predicted daily change.
- Skill against persistence: 1 − MAE(model) / MAE(persistence). Above 0 means the model beats "tomorrow's price equals today's" (predicted change 0); 0 or below is the expected result for daily prices and is reported as such.
- Directional accuracy: share of days on which the predicted sign of the change is correct.

Operation of the running system:

- Prediction latency (95th percentile) and error rate of the API.
- Data freshness: trading days after the latest stored day that were final when the security's latest load ran.
- Missed daily updates: scheduled daily updates after the latest load whose load limit, the longest a load may run, has passed; left out while the replay database exists.
- Drift p-value: the p-value of each drift check; drift is found when the p-value is at or below the drift p-value threshold.
- Training runs: duration and outcome (succeeded, promoted, kept as candidate).

Threshold values for alerts and drift are configuration, set by the team.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: How requirements are checked

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Each requirement names how it is checked (VERIFICATION):

- Test: an automated black-box test calls the system through its public interfaces (API, commands, database) and names the requirement it checks.
- Demonstration: shown on the running system, because it depends on time passing or on a dashboard.
- Inspection: checked by review of the repository and its configuration; this covers the constraints set by the course.

Design choices and the schedule are not requirements; they are recorded in the plan and the decision documents.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: What the product supports

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
- One local machine per team member, running the whole system with Docker Compose; no cloud service and no machine shared between members.
- Python 3.12, with the environment managed by uv.
- Docker Engine 28.0 or later (Docker Desktop includes it).
- Market data from EODHD with the member's own key; the reference securities (six stocks, two market indices) fit the free tier's 20 calls per day with one load or update per day.
- Every service listens on the local machine only (127.0.0.1).
- Alert thresholds and collection intervals are set in the project's own files, never in a member's environment file.
- Of the daily update and replay pipelines, only one is switched on at a time.
- At most one load or replay runs at a time, scheduled or manual; a manual one runs only while the daily update and replay pipelines are paused.
- At most one training runs at a time, whether scheduled, started because drift was found, or manual; a manual one runs only while the training pipeline is paused.
- A missed scheduled run is not repeated; the next daily update fetches from the latest stored day.
- Not guarded against: anyone or anything on the member's own machine — another account, program or web page; every service is published on 127.0.0.1 only, or not at all.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Data

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-DAT-001
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-1
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Historical load
STATEMENT: >>>
The system loads the daily price history (open, high, low, close, volume) from a configured first day on of each configured security and market index, and each security's splits and dividends, into its database in a single run. Prices and volumes are stored as traded on each day, not adjusted for later splits or dividends.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-DAT-002
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Daily ingestion
STATEMENT: >>>
The system adds the quotes of each new trading day to its database, fetching only the days from its latest stored quote on.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-DAT-003
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Historical replay
STATEMENT: >>>
The system can replay stored history one trading day at a time, as if each day were arriving live, into a database of its own, at an interval set by the operator: one trading day every 10 to 60 seconds. The history it replays from stays unchanged. While the replay database exists, training, forecasts, price history and model results use it, and training and forecasts keep their runs and models apart from the member's own; resetting the replay deletes the replay database and those runs and models.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Shows the complete loop of ingestion, drift check, retraining and promotion within minutes instead of weeks.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-DAT-004
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-1
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Trading calendar
STATEMENT: >>>
The system counts only trading days of the security's exchange; weekends, public holidays and trading suspensions are not treated as missing data.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-DAT-005
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-1
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Validation of delivered data
STATEMENT: >>>
The system rejects a delivered quote, split or dividend with a missing field, a non-positive price, ratio or amount, or a day delivered twice in one delivery before it is stored, and records the rejection. It also rejects a quote with a negative volume or on a day that is not a trading day of its exchange.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-DAT-006
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Dataset versioning
STATEMENT: >>>
Every dataset used for training has a version identifier, and every trained model records the identifier of the dataset it was trained on.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-DAT-007
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-1
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Provisional closes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system stores each quote with the time it was fetched. A quote fetched before a set delay after its exchange's close of that trading day is provisional and is replaced by a later fetch of the same day; a quote fetched after that is final and is never replaced.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The data source delivers the current day while its session is still running, in the same form as a finished day.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Model

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOD-001
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-1
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Forecast target
STATEMENT: >>>
The model predicts the close-to-close change of a configured security from the latest trading day to the next trading day, with closes corrected for splits. It is trained on final closes only.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOD-002
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-1
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Baselines
STATEMENT: >>>
Every evaluation also scores two baselines on the same data: persistence (tomorrow's price equals today's, i.e. a predicted change of 0) and the historical mean change.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOD-003
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-1
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: No look-ahead
STATEMENT: >>>
Features for a predicted day use only data dated before that day, and evaluation data is always later in time than training data.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOD-004
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Experiment tracking
STATEMENT: >>>
Every training run records its parameters, metrics, dataset version, code version, resulting model and whether that model became the production model.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOD-005
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Model promotion
STATEMENT: >>>
A newly trained model becomes the production model only if it is better than the current production model by the agreed rule; otherwise the current production model stays in place. The first model trained for a security becomes its production model.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MOD-006
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Training when needed
STATEMENT: >>>
A training request that asks to train only when needed trains a security only when it has no recorded training, when the drift check of REQ-MON-001 finds drift, or when at least the configured number of trading days have been stored since its latest training; the response says whether it trained and why. Any other request always trains.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Service

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-SVC-001
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-1
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Prediction endpoint
STATEMENT: >>>
The API returns the production model's forecast for the next trading day of a requested security, together with the model version that produced it, the close the forecast starts from and the time that close was fetched. A symbol that is not a configured security, or a configured security without a production model, is refused.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-SVC-002
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-1
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Training endpoint
STATEMENT: >>>
The API starts a training run on request, or skips it as REQ-MOD-006 states for a request that asks to train only when needed, and reports the outcome. A symbol that is not a configured security is refused.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-SVC-003
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Prediction log
STATEMENT: >>>
The system stores every forecast it makes, through the API or a command, with its input features, the model version and the time of request.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-SVC-004
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2, optional
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Access control
STATEMENT: >>>
The API answers only authenticated callers; starting a training and managing users are reserved for administrators.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-SVC-005
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Securities endpoint
STATEMENT: >>>
The API lists every configured security.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-SVC-006
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Price history endpoint
STATEMENT: >>>
The API returns the closes of a configured security's latest stored trading days, oldest first and corrected for splits: as many days as the caller asks for, all of them where fewer are stored; the latest close may be provisional. A symbol that is not a configured security is refused.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-SVC-007
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Model results endpoint
STATEMENT: >>>
The API returns, for a configured security, the version of its production model and the number of evaluation days of that model's training run. It also returns the MAE, skill against persistence and directional accuracy of the model and of both baselines on those days. Where that run recorded it, it also returns the change that the mean-change baseline forecasts. A symbol that is not a configured security, or a configured security without a production model, is refused.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Automation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUT-001
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Scheduled training pipeline
STATEMENT: >>>
On a configured schedule, the system ingests new quotes, runs training when needed (REQ-MOD-006), forecasts each configured security and checks the forecasts for drift (REQ-MON-002), without manual steps. When drift is found in the forecasts, a training of every configured security starts. A failed run shows its reason on the pipeline's page.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUT-002
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Outcome collection
STATEMENT: >>>
Once a predicted day's actual quote is stored, the system records it against each forecast for that day and computes the production error.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUT-003
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: One-command start
STATEMENT: >>>
The complete system starts with one command from a fresh clone of the repository, each component running as a separate service.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUT-004
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2, optional
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Continuous integration
STATEMENT: >>>
Every push runs linting, type checks and unit tests; a scheduled check builds the project image and runs the acceptance tests.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUT-005
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Commands from any folder
STATEMENT: >>>
Each command of the system works the same whatever folder it is started from.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUT-006
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Packaged environments from one lock file
STATEMENT: >>>
The system's commands, and its services built from its own code, run in packaged environments installed from the pinned package versions of the project's single lock file.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUT-007
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Configured values checked at start
STATEMENT: >>>
A configured value, in the member's environment file or the project's configuration folder, that is missing or outside its allowed range makes the commands and services that read it refuse to start, with a message that names the setting.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AUT-008
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-2
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Training continues past a failed security
STATEMENT: >>>
A run of the training pipeline goes through every configured security, training it or not as REQ-MOD-006 decides, even when the training of one of them fails; the run then fails and names each security whose training failed.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Monitoring

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MON-001
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Feature drift
STATEMENT: >>>
Every training of a security that has a recorded training compares the daily price changes of the latest configured number of stored trading days with those of all stored trading days up to its latest training, and records the drift report and its p-value. Drift is found when the p-value is at or below the configured value.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MON-002
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Prediction drift
STATEMENT: >>>
A drift check of a security's scheduled forecasts runs when the security has no earlier such check or when at least the configured number of trading days have been stored since its latest one. It takes, for each of the latest configured number of days with a scheduled forecast, that day's last one, has the production model forecast again from its stored inputs, and compares the results with that model's forecasts for all stored trading days up to the security's latest training. It records the drift report and its p-value and answers whether drift is found (as REQ-MON-001 defines it). A security with fewer days that have a scheduled forecast is not checked, and the answer says why.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MON-003
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Service metrics and dashboard
STATEMENT: >>>
The system collects request count, latency and error rate of the API and shows them, together with data freshness and, for each security, the latest result of each of its two drift checks (REQ-MON-001, REQ-MON-002), on a dashboard.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MON-004
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
TITLE: Alerts
STATEMENT: >>>
The system raises an alert when a monitored metric crosses its configured threshold.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MON-005
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Training started by an alert
STATEMENT: >>>
An alert configured to start training starts the training pipeline.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Web app

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-APP-001
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Forecast view
STATEMENT: >>>
The web app lets a user choose a security and shows the closes of its latest 60 trading days, the model's forecast for the next trading day and the forecasts of the persistence and mean-change baselines, each as a change and the close it leads to; the mean-change forecast only if the training run recorded it. For a security without a production model, the web app shows the API's reason for giving no forecast. When the API fails on a request, the web app shows the API's reason instead.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-APP-002
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Not investment advice
STATEMENT: >>>
Every page of the web app states that the forecasts are not investment advice.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-APP-003
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: phase-3
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Model results
STATEMENT: >>>
The web app shows the MAE, skill against persistence and directional accuracy of the production model next to those of both baselines.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Course constraints

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CON-001
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: course
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Prescribed tools
STATEMENT: >>>
The system uses the tools the course prescribes: MLflow for experiment tracking and the model registry, DVC without Git for dataset versions (hashes recorded in MLflow), Docker Compose for the services, Airflow for scheduled pipelines and drift checks, Evidently for drift reports, Prometheus and Grafana for service monitoring and alerts, and an SQL or NoSQL database.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CON-002
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: course
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Local operation
STATEMENT: >>>
The complete system, including its database, runs on a local machine without any cloud service.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-CON-003
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: course
VERIFICATION: Inspection
TITLE: Database as the data store
STATEMENT: >>>
The system keeps all the data it uses in its database; files fetched from a data source are only read into the database, never used as storage. DVC snapshots are version records of training datasets, never a store that data is read from.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
